      ],
      "id": "7r22nrk"
    },
    {
      "id": "rwirn9h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nutrition encompasses sequential steps starting from food intake to digestion and assimilation.",
        "Carbohydrates, proteins, and fats constitute the major energy-yielding macronutrients.",
        "Vitamins and minerals serve as essential micronutrients vital for cellular functions and immunity.",
        "A balanced diet is essential to maintain optimal health and prevent deficiency syndromes.",
        "Malnutrition encompasses both undernutrition and overnutrition, leading to common nutritional disorders."
      ],
      "id": "jycuer1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4j3eavq",
      "content": "• Nutrition is the process of obtaining food and utilizing it for energy and body functions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wwq3k0a",
      "content": "• It includes ingestion, digestion, absorption, assimilation and excretion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "19ik75o",
      "content": "• Good nutrition helps maintain physical and mental health."
    },
    {
      "id": "ogj0vjt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Steps in Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yi1ulrf",
      "content": "• Ingestion – Taking food into the body."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wb1llp6",
      "content": "• Digestion – Breaking down complex food into simple molecules."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xhantc0",
      "content": "• Absorption – Nutrients enter the bloodstream through the intestine."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2rcqg39",
      "content": "• Assimilation – Nutrients used by cells for energy and growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d0avuue",
      "content": "• Egestion – Removal of undigested waste."
    },
    {
